# chorus golden vector: handshake init, protocol v2 message type 0x20.
#
# Committed, and never written by a test. Any implementation of chorus protocol v2 must
# produce these exact bytes from the canonical input in handshake_init.fields, and recover
# exactly those fields from them (docs/protocol.md, "Version 2").
#
# Format: whitespace separated hex bytes, '#' starts a comment.
# Test-only keys (the four X25519 secrets in the .fields file) are public: never use them
# for a real device. The Noise prologue is the 7 bytes of handshake_init before the Noise
# message: 43 48 52 53 00 02 01. Noise_XX_25519_ChaChaPoly_SHA256 (noiseprotocol.org, rev 34).

# frame header: type 0x20, payload length 39 (0x0027), big-endian
20 00 27

# magic = ASCII CHRS
43 48 52 53

# protocol_version = 2
00 02

# suite = 1 (Noise_XX_25519_ChaChaPoly_SHA256)
01

# noise: Noise message 1 (-> e): the endpoint's ephemeral public key, empty payload
34 E4 2D 4A F5 EF 94 A0 7A 3A 84 20 1B 88 9D 4C
D1 A7 43 CB 27 B1 1B 6A 10 43 8A 8F EB 8E 58 47
